Braces enumerate every named file, not an entire package.

V2 shader ports (also used/modified by V3–V4)
------------------------------------------
Each of the following local files derives from the identical upstream shader
path, except the explicit blit extension mappings:
- lod/{block_model.glsl,frustum.glsl,lighting.glsl,pos_util.glsl,quad_format.glsl,quad_util.glsl,section.glsl}
- lod/hierarchical/{node.glsl,queue.glsl,screenspace.glsl,traversal_dev.comp}
- lod/hierarchical/cleaner/{batch_visibility_set.comp,result_transformer.comp,sort_visibility.comp}
- lod/gl46/{bindings.glsl,prep.comp,cmdgen.comp,buildtranslucents.comp,quads3.vert,quads.frag}
- lod/gl46/cull/{raster.vert,raster.frag}
- hiz/hiz.comp
- hiz/blit.vert <- hiz/blit.vsh
- hiz/blit.frag <- hiz/blit.fsh
- util/{depthutils.glsl,memcpy.comp,scatter.comp}
- util/prefixsum/{inital3.comp,simple.comp}

Ports replace GL bindings with Vulkan descriptors, push constants and built-ins.
HiZ retains the clustered subgroup algorithm with a shared-memory fallback.
V3 bounds indirect-command writes to their allocated regions. Upstream shader
resources do not carry file-level license blocks; port headers identify their
upstream paths. lod/gl46/fog.glsl and lod/depth_convert.{vert,frag} are JBP-LOD
Vulkan additions, not copies of upstream shaders; the depth conversion replaces
the role of upstream post/depth_cp.* rather than porting its GL framebuffer copy.

